    "tiptap_body": {
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Claude forgets and large chunks of long chats can disappear.  From now on, when I do a long chat with Claude, I will assume I must capture the knowledge gained, issues overcome, and the solutions.  Fortunately with Kortex installed, a button appears on claude chats “notebook LM”.  Clicking that pulls the whole chat into a notebook.  In NLM, I can tell it to summarize all that was learned, and prepare a syllabus to teach it.  And I can take that result in put it in the claude project files or instructions.  I’m sure there are many ways to do similar compressing, but I will be keeping this in my toolbag.  ",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "Claude forgets and large chunks of long chats can disappear.  From now on, when I do a long chat with Claude, I will assume I must capture the knowledge gained, issues overcome, and the solutions.  Fortunately with Kortex installed, a button appears on claude chats “notebook LM”.  Clicking that pulls the whole chat into a notebook.  In NLM, I can tell it to summarize all that was learned, and prepare a syllabus to teach it.  And I can take that result in put it in the claude project files or instructions.  I’m sure there are many ways to do similar compressing, but I will be keeping this in my toolbag.  "
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
